{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"c3683224b02fb97d1c4e9d17aa7fe39f32f47a343d0058943656c663c8cf1f4a","digest":{"component_or_area":"LLM provider resolution","key_entities":["_resolve_target","infer_provider","split_provider_qualifier","model_classes._resolve_target","config.infer_provider","_PROVIDER_QUALIFIER_RE","bedrock provider","anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0","us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6"],"problem_keywords":["bedrock","model id","provider qualifier","colon separator","silent drop","canonical versioned id"],"propositions":["A configured provider is silently discarded when a model id contains a colon anywhere in the string, not only as a provider separator","Canonical Bedrock versioned ids like 'us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0' contain a colon in the version suffix and fail to resolve to the configured 'bedrock' provider","The qualifier detection logic treats any colon as evidence of an already-qualified string and returns unmodified, losing the explicit provider configuration","An explicitly configured provider must be checked and honoured before any parsing or inference of the model string occurs","A conflict between an inline qualifier and a configured provider should raise an error naming both rather than silently picking one"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787297156866727001,"uuid":"1a6330cc-a5e1-473a-bc6b-414cfedd16cb"}